&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to creating a space where our employees can bring their full selves to work and have equal opportunity to succeed. No matter your race, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, origin, ability, age, veteran status, if joining this mission speaks to you, we encourage you to apply!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Head of Sales, Digital Native to build and lead the sales organization covering the fastest-growing segment of our business: digital native and AI-native companies building on voice. Today this is a small, high-performing team selling into a targeted list of the best accounts building with voice. You will scale it into a multi-layer organization of Account Executives and the front-line managers who lead them, while growing revenue across AssemblyAI&#39;s Voice AI models, orchestration like our Voice Agent API, and LLM Gateway.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder&#39;s role, not a caretaker&#39;s. You will own the hiring bar, the org design, the territory and target account model, the comp plans, and the operating cadence for the segment. You will personally recruit and develop the first wave of front-line managers, and you&#39;ll be accountable for making a scaling AE org productive fast - not just filling seats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to the VP of Customer Solutions and work in tight partnership with Applied AI Engineering, Forward Deployed Engineering, Marketing, Engineering, and Research. Our motion is technical, product-led, and evaluation-driven: customers choose us because we win benchmarks and ship the best customer experience. Your team&#39;s job is to get in front of the right builders early, build relationships, get them to run an evals, and convert wins into production usage that compounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the digital native sales organization - scaling from a small team of AEs and BDRs today to a larger sales org within the next year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the land number for the segment, focusing on bringing in net new customers and helping them scale up their usage in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, onboard, and develop front-line managers; establish the bar, the interview loop, and the ramp plan that make new AEs productive in weeks rather than quarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the segment&#39;s coverage model - territories, target account tiers, and specialization across a large digital native account list where every company has a real production voice use case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operating system for the team: forecasting, pipeline inspection, deal reviews, quota and comp design, and the metrics that tell you early whether the org is on track&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Applied AI Engineering and Forward Deployed Engineering on the eval-to-production motion, so technical wins convert into deployed, growing usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering, Research, and Marketing to shorten the time from product launch to real revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive an outbound-first culture where pipeline is created, not waited for, and where outreach earns replies through custom benchmarks, competitive insight, and use-case-specific demos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the digital native voice of the customer to the leadership team and shape go-to-market strategy as new products launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in technical sales with 4+ years leading sales teams, including experience managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of scaling a sales org through a step change in headcount - you have hired and ramped 10+ reps and built the management layer underneath you, not inherited it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling infrastructure, APIs, or developer platforms to engineering and product buyers; ideally in a usage-based or consumption pricing model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with a product-led, bottoms-up motion that layers a sales team on top of self-serve adoption without breaking what already works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical credibility - comfortable discussing API architectures, model accuracy tradeoffs, latency, and deployment options directly with engineers and CTOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design territories, quotas, and comp plans that drive the right behavior, and to run a forecast leadership can rely on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recruiting instinct - you carry your own network, you close candidates, and you hold a high bar under pressure to fill seats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High urgency and comfort with ambiguity; this segment and its product lines are changing quickly and the playbook is being written as you scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to travel to drive impact - expect to be on the road 50%+ of each month for customer visits, industry events, and team offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
